course: dictionary
lesson: 5348
title: A very hot oven
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A kiln is a very hot oven. Potters use it to bake clay so that it becomes hard. «Pottery is different: soft clay is shaped and then baked in a very hot oven called a kiln until it turns hard as stone.» The sentence gives you the clues: very hot, oven, baked, and hard as stone.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «soft clay is shaped and then baked in a very hot oven called a very hot oven until it turns hard as stone.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Kilns are not only for pottery. The meaning also says a kiln can dry things like wood or hops. The phrases «pottery kiln» and «brick kiln» show what kind of kiln you are talking about.
explain: A kiln is extremely hot, so only adults use one. «The kiln is only for adults because it is extremely hot.» If you ever see a kiln, stay back and ask a grown-up.
fact: A kiln is a very hot oven used for baking (firing) clay pots, bricks or tiles.
fact: Baking clay in a kiln makes it hard, and the change is permanent: «pottery does not turn back into mud».
fact: Kilns can also be used to dry things like wood or hops.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «fire in a kiln», «pottery kiln» and «brick kiln».
fact: Kilns are extremely hot, so only adults use them.
exercise: «Pottery is clay baked in a kiln at a very high heat.» What is a kiln? | A cold cupboard for storing paint | A small pot for tea | A type of glue | *A very hot oven used for baking clay
exercise: «Baking clay in a kiln changes its minerals for good.» What does for good mean here? | *Permanently, so it cannot change back | Just for fun | For a good reason | For a short time only
exercise: Why are only adults allowed to use a kiln? | Because it makes loud music | *Because it is extremely hot | Because it is very heavy to lift | Because it is full of paint
test: Which thing is made hard by baking it in a kiln? | A balloon | A sheet of paper | A bowl of soup | *A clay tile
test: «A brick kiln» is a kiln used for which job? | Building a wall with bricks | *Baking bricks in a very hot oven | Selling bricks in a shop | Painting bricks bright colours
exam: Why must children never use a kiln on their own? | *Because it is extremely hot, so only adults use it | Because it takes days to switch on | Because it is too light to hold steady | Because it is only for drying paint
